, and a weight decay of 0.01. Training was carried out over seven epochs using the Hugging Face Transformers library and NVIDIA Tesla P100 GPUs available on Kaggle. The model's performance was assessed using 5-fold cross- validation, resulting in impressive metrics: an average accuracy of 99.34 percent, precision of 99.36 percent, recall of 99.34 percent, F1-score of 99.34 percent, and an ROC-AUC score of 99.96 percent. These results highlight the model's effectiveness in identifying hate speech and offensive content across different data splits. Compared to earlier research, this approach shows significant improvement in performance metrics. It demonstrates the potential of combining BERT with data augmentation and oversampling techniques for detecting hate speech in political discourse on Reddit. This study lays the groundwork for future research into real-time detection systems and cross-lingual models.","publicationDate":"20 November 2024","pdfPath":"/iel8/10787129/10787157/10787162.pdf","publicationYear":"2024","displayPublicationTitle":"2024 22nd International Conference on ICT and Knowledge Engineering (ICT&KE)","pdfUrl":"/stamp/stamp.jsp?tp=&arnumber=10787162","startPage":"1","endPage":"8","publicationTitle":"2024 22nd International Conference on ICT and Knowledge Engineering (ICT&KE)","formulaStrippedArticleTitle":"Fine-Tuned BERT Model for Hate Speech Detection in Political Discourse","keywords":[{"type":"IEEE Keywords","kwd":["Analytical models","Social networking (online)","Hate speech","Training data","Bidirectional control","Transformers","Data augmentation","Encoding","Natural language processing","Data models"]},{"type":"Index Terms","kwd":["Political Discourse","Detection Model","Hate Speech","Hate Speech Detection","Social Media","Model Performance","Learning Rate","Batch Size","Performance Metrics","Online Communities","Data Augmentation","Weight Decay","Data Split","5-fold Cross","Natural Language Processing Techniques","Overfitting","Twitter","A